  "plain": "Filippo Biondi, a researcher who has been scanning the ground beneath the pyramids at Giza in Egypt, told podcast host Jesse Michels in 2026 about what his work in the 2020s has found. He says his team counts four plus four tube-like shapes running downward under a pyramid, linking its base to something located far below. If true, it would mean the pyramids sit on top of a large, deliberately built structure underground."
